    <div class="bio-content"><h2>My story</h2><p class="body-large">I’m Kastine Augak, a software-minded entrepreneur and creative based in Uganda. My interests sit at the intersection of technology, business, research and communication.</p><p>I’m interested in how digital products can make everyday work easier, how emerging technologies can serve local communities, and how ideas can be communicated clearly. I approach projects with curiosity, practical problem-solving and a desire to keep learning.</p><p>This website is the central place for my professional work and personal interests. It will continue to grow as projects develop and new work becomes ready to share.</p>
    <div class="bio-divider"></div><section id="ventures"><p class="eyebrow">01 / VENTURES & BUILDING</p><h2>Making digital ideas tangible</h2><p>My work includes software development and digital product exploration, alongside business and technology initiatives such as Apex Web Services, SomaGPT and Soma Analytics. Each represents an interest in applying technology to practical needs. Details and public project links will be added as they are verified and ready to share.</p></section>
    <div class="bio-divider"></div><section id="research"><p class="eyebrow">02 / RESEARCH & LEARNING</p><h2>Questions worth exploring</h2><p>I’m particularly interested in AI, data, language technology and digital access. One long-term area of exploration is language technology for local Ugandan languages, including work around Rutooro and accessible digital knowledge.</p></section>
    <div class="bio-divider"></div><section><p class="eyebrow">03 / CREATIVE INTERESTS</p><h2>Technology is also culture</h2><p>Music, storytelling and digital media are important parts of how I explore and share ideas. I enjoy connecting technical subjects with everyday experiences and making complex topics easier to understand.</p></section>
    <div class="bio-divider"></div><section><p class="eyebrow">04 / VALUES</p><h2>What guides the work</h2><ul class="values-list"><li>Build for real needs, not just appearances.</li><li>Keep experiences accessible and respectful of people’s time and data.</li><li>Stay curious, test assumptions and keep improving.</li><li>Make room for local context and global collaboration.</li></ul></section>
